import json
R=[
("Q102272","Jan van Eyck was a Flemish painter born around 1390 who worked for the Duke of Burgundy and lived in Bruges until he died in 1441. He was a master of oil paint, using thin glowing layers to paint jewels, fabric and reflections in amazing detail. His Arnolfini Portrait and the Ghent Altarpiece are among the most famous pictures of the 1400s."),
("Q1056977","Cesare da Sesto was an Italian painter born around 1477 near Milan. He studied the work of Leonardo da Vinci, whose soft shading and gentle faces he copied, and later worked in Rome and southern Italy. He died in 1523."),
("Q1066580","Charles de La Fosse was a French painter born in Paris in 1636. He studied in Italy and became known for big, colorful decorations in the churches and palaces of Louis XIV, including the dome of Les Invalides in Paris. He died in Paris in 1716."),
("Q106851","Hans Memling was born in Germany in about 1435 and became the most successful painter in Bruges, in what is now Belgium. His calm, sweet and beautifully detailed religious pictures and portraits were bought by rich merchants and bankers from all over Europe. He died in Bruges in 1494."),
("Q107308387","Konstantinos Tzanes was a painter from the Greek island of Crete, born in 1633. Like many Cretan painters, he moved to Venice, where he mixed the Greek icon tradition with Italian art. He died there in 1685."),
("Q109061","Guido Reni was an Italian painter born in Bologna in 1575. He became one of the most admired artists of the Baroque, known for graceful figures, soft light and pretty faces in his religious and mythological scenes. He died in Bologna in 1642."),
("Q1269439","Federico Benković was a painter born in about 1677 in Dalmatia, on the Adriatic coast of today's Croatia. He trained in Bologna and Venice and later worked in Croatia and Slovenia. He died in 1753."),
("Q1345289","Giovanni Battista Salvi, called Sassoferrato after his home town, was an Italian painter born in 1609. He painted many sweet, smooth pictures of Mary, with deep blue robes, in a style that looked back to Raphael. He died in Rome in 1685."),
("Q1357759","Lambert Sustris was a painter born in Amsterdam around 1515 who moved to Italy and worked in Venice and Padua. He painted portraits, myths and big landscapes in the style of Titian, whom he worked with. He died in 1584."),
("Q142398","Francesco Rosselli was an engraver, painter and map maker born in Florence in about 1445. He is best known for his early views and maps of cities, including a view of Naples. He died in 1513."),
("Q154338","Matthias Grünewald was a German painter born in about 1480. His religious paintings have strong colors and powerful emotions, and his Isenheim Altarpiece is one of the greatest works of German art. He died in Halle in 1528."),
("Q155575","Martin Schongauer was a German painter and engraver born in Colmar around 1440. His detailed prints were copied across Europe, and the young Albrecht Dürer wanted to meet him. He died in Breisach in 1491."),
("Q164696","Hans Baldung Grien was a German painter and printmaker born around 1480. He worked with Albrecht Dürer in Nuremberg, and is known for strange pictures of witches, death and nudes. He died in Strasbourg in 1545."),
("Q167654","Frans Hals was a Dutch painter who was born in Antwerp around 1582 and lived most of his life in Haarlem. He painted lively portraits with fast, loose brushstrokes, so his sitters seem to laugh, drink and talk right in front of you. He died in Haarlem in 1666."),
("Q183458","Andrea del Verrocchio was an Italian sculptor and painter born in Florence in about 1435. His busy workshop trained many famous artists, including Leonardo da Vinci. He died in Venice in 1488."),
("Q184669","Jean Ranc was a French portrait painter born in Montpellier in 1674. He worked at the court in Madrid, where he painted the Spanish royal family. He died there in 1735."),
("Q19034","Arent de Gelder, also known as Aert, was born in Dordrecht, in the Netherlands, in 1645. He studied with Rembrandt and kept painting in Rembrandt's rich, thick style long after his teacher's death. He died in 1727."),
("Q191423","Domenico Ghirlandaio was a Florentine painter born in 1448. He painted busy, lively frescoes of Bible stories set in Florence with its real people, and he ran a big workshop that included the young Michelangelo. He died in 1494."),
("Q192062","Bartolomé Esteban Murillo was a Spanish painter born in Seville in 1617. He painted soft, warm pictures of Mary and the saints and also lovely scenes of poor children in the street. He died in Seville in 1682."),
("Q192488","Paolo Uccello was a Florentine painter born in about 1397. He was so crazy about the new science of perspective that he filled his pictures with lances, broken spears and tiled floors that line up to a point. He died in 1475."),
("Q203371","Georges de La Tour was a French painter born in 1593 in Lorraine. He is known for quiet night scenes lit by a single candle, with smooth, simple shapes. He died in 1652, and was almost forgotten until the 1900s."),
("Q205148","Filippo Lippi was a Florentine painter born in 1406, who was a Carmelite friar for much of his life. He painted tender Madonnas with real, lovely faces, and his son Filippino also became a painter. He died in Spoleto in 1469."),
("Q205863","Jan Steen was a Dutch painter born in Leiden in 1626. He painted lively, messy family scenes and parties full of jokes and lessons, so much that a messy home is called a Jan Steen household in Dutch. He died in 1679."),
("Q209615","Francisco de Zurbarán was a Spanish painter born in 1598. He painted monks, saints and still lifes with strong light and deep shadows, and a calm, simple look. He died in Madrid in 1664."),
("Q2116186","Albert Eckhout was a Dutch painter born in about 1610. He was sent to Brazil in 1637 by a Dutch governor, and he painted the people, plants and animals he saw there in great detail. He died in 1666."),
("Q212593","Hendrick Avercamp was a Dutch painter born in Amsterdam in 1585. He was deaf and could not speak, and became famous for his crowded winter scenes of people skating and playing on ice. He died in Kampen in 1634."),
("Q212657","Artemisia Gentileschi was an Italian painter born in Rome in 1593, the daughter of the painter Orazio Gentileschi. She was one of the first women to become a successful professional painter in Europe, and her powerful pictures often show strong women from the Bible and myths. She died in Naples in about 1653."),
("Q213612","Jacob van Ruisdael was a Dutch landscape painter born in Haarlem in 1628. He painted windmills, forests, waterfalls and giant stormy skies, and his work inspired later painters like John Constable. He died in 1682."),
("Q215251","Hugo van der Goes was a Flemish painter born in Ghent around 1440. His large, emotional altarpieces were admired by Italian artists, and later in life he joined a monastery. He died in 1482."),
("Q217715","Caspar Netscher was a Dutch painter born in 1635 in Heidelberg, Germany. He became famous for small portraits and indoor scenes with beautiful, shiny silks and satins. He died in The Hague in 1684."),
("Q2273503","Niccolò Antonio Colantonio was a painter from Naples, born around 1420. He was influenced by Flemish painters and taught Antonello da Messina. He died in about 1460."),
("Q232423","Judith Leyster was a Dutch painter born in Haarlem in 1609. She painted lively scenes of musicians and everyday people and was one of the few women admitted to the painters' guild. After she died in 1660 her work was mistaken for Frans Hals's until it was rediscovered in the 1890s."),
("Q2327761","Gianfrancesco Penni was an Italian painter born in Florence in about 1488. He was one of the main helpers in Raphael's workshop in Rome and helped finish Raphael's work after he died. He later worked in Naples."),
("Q236038","Sofonisba Anguissola was an Italian painter born in Cremona in 1532. She was one of the first women artists to become famous across Europe, and worked as a court painter for the king of Spain. She lived to the age of about 93 and died in Palermo in 1625."),
("Q237726","Rosalba Carriera was a Venetian painter born in 1675, who was famous for portraits in soft pastel chalk. She was welcomed in Paris, Vienna and Venice, and she was one of the first women to be admitted to the French Academy. She died in 1757."),
("Q25710346","Jacques Laumosnier was a French painter born in Paris in 1669, who worked as a painter of history and portraits. He died in Paris in 1744."),
("Q265398","Clara Peeters was a Flemish painter, born in Antwerp in about 1587. She was one of the first women to paint still lifes, with beautiful shiny dishes, cheese, flowers and food, and she sometimes hid a tiny reflection of herself in them. She died in about 1657."),
("Q269338","Josefa de Óbidos was a painter born in Seville in 1630, who grew up and worked in Portugal. She painted religious pictures and still lifes and was one of the best-known Portuguese painters of her time. She died in 1684."),
("Q280851","Piero di Cosimo was a Florentine painter born in 1461. He liked painting mythical stories with strange creatures and wild nature, and he had a reputation as an eccentric who lived on hard-boiled eggs. He died in 1522."),
("Q2824028","Adam Willaerts was a Dutch painter born in London in 1577, who settled in Utrecht. He painted busy seascapes, beaches and ships, and he died in 1664."),
("Q290812","Stefan Lochner was a German painter born in about 1410, who worked in Cologne. His sweet, gold-and-jewel-bright pictures, like the Madonna of the Rose Bower, made him the most famous painter of Cologne. He died in 1451."),
("Q29447","Cosimo Rosselli was a Florentine painter born in 1439. He was one of the artists invited to Rome to paint the walls of the Sistine Chapel in the 1480s. He died in 1507."),
("Q296265","Filippino Lippi was a Florentine painter born in Prato in 1457. He was the son of the painter Filippo Lippi and trained with Botticelli, and is known for graceful, elegant figures. He died in Florence in 1504."),
("Q297838","Jusepe de Ribera was a Spanish painter, born in 1591, who spent most of his life in Naples. His dramatic pictures of saints, philosophers and beggars use strong light and dark. He died in Naples in 1652."),
("Q301","El Greco, whose name means The Greek, was born on the island of Crete in 1541 and moved to Spain, where he lived in Toledo. He painted long, twisting figures with flickering light and brilliant colors, quite unlike anyone else of his time. He died in 1614."),
("Q302062","Antonio Bellucci was an Italian painter born in 1654, who worked in Venice, Vienna and England. He painted religious scenes and myths with warm color. He died in 1726."),
("Q304411","Melchior d'Hondecoeter was a Dutch painter born in Utrecht in 1636. He specialized in painting birds, such as peacocks, roosters and ducks, in lively, feathery pictures. He died in Amsterdam in 1695."),
("Q310285","Adam Elsheimer was a German painter born in Frankfurt in 1578. He worked in Rome painting tiny, jewel-like pictures with moonlight, firelight and stars, and he influenced Rembrandt and Rubens. He died in 1610."),
("Q310973","Lorenzo Lotto was a Venetian painter born in 1480, who traveled a lot and painted psychologically sharp portraits. His religious paintings have a quirky charm. He died in Loreto in 1556."),
("Q311082","Pisanello was an Italian painter and medal maker, born in about 1395. He painted elegant, detailed pictures of knights, ladies and animals for noble courts, and he invented the portrait medal. He died in about 1455."),
("Q312616","Petrus Christus was a Flemish painter, born around 1410 in Baarle. He lived in Bruges and followed in the footsteps of Jan van Eyck, with calm, clear pictures. He died in 1475."),
("Q312617","Rosso Fiorentino was a Florentine painter born in 1494 with wild red hair. He painted jagged, strange and colorful pictures, and went to France to decorate the palace at Fontainebleau for King Francis I. He died there in 1540."),
("Q313183","Konrad Witz was a German-Swiss painter born in about 1400 who worked in Basel. His pictures of solid, heavy figures in real landscapes were ahead of their time. He died in about 1445."),
("Q313561","Dieric Bouts was a Dutch painter born in Haarlem around 1410 who moved to Leuven, in modern Belgium. He painted quiet, sad figures in carefully drawn rooms and landscapes. He died in 1475."),
("Q314275","Quinten Metsys was a painter from Leuven, who worked in Antwerp. He made realistic scenes of everyday life, from moneylenders to funny old women, and helped make Antwerp a great art center. He died in 1530."),
("Q314548","Gerard van Honthorst was a Dutch painter born in Utrecht in 1592. He went to Rome and learned from Caravaggio's use of light, and became known for night scenes lit by a single candle. He died in 1656."),
("Q314889","Pieter de Hooch was a Dutch painter born in Rotterdam in 1629. He painted peaceful scenes of Dutch homes and courtyards, with careful perspective and bright sunlight. He died in Amsterdam in 1683."),
("Q316731","Federico Barocci was an Italian painter born in Urbino in 1535. He painted soft, warm, sweet pictures of the Holy Family with pink and blue colors and loving faces. He died in 1612."),
("Q317920","Simon Vouet was a French painter born in Paris in 1590. He spent years in Italy, where he learned the dramatic style, and then returned to France to become the king's painter. He died in Paris in 1649."),
("Q318640","Antonio del Pollaiuolo was a Florentine artist born in 1429, who was a painter, goldsmith and sculptor. He studied the human body in action, and was one of the first to examine dead bodies to learn how muscles work. He died in Rome in 1498."),
("Q320980","Lucas van Leyden was a Dutch painter and printmaker born in Leiden in 1494. He began making prints as a child and became one of the best engravers of his time. He died in 1533."),
("Q326548","Pieter Aertsen was a Dutch painter born in Amsterdam in 1508. He painted huge market scenes with mountains of food in the front, and tiny Bible scenes in the back. He died in 1575."),
("Q3290536","Margaretha Haverman was a Dutch painter born in Breda in 1693, who painted flower pictures. She moved to Paris and was admitted to the French Academy in 1722, but was soon accused of fraud and left. She died in about 1723."),
("Q332494","Luca Giordano was a Neapolitan painter, born in 1632. He painted so fast that people called him Luca Fa Presto, Luca Work Fast. His huge, swirling ceilings and altarpieces decorated palaces and churches in Italy and Spain. He died in Naples in 1705."),
("Q333380","Gerard David was a Dutch painter born in about 1460. He worked in Bruges and became the city's top painter after Hans Memling died. He died in 1523."),
("Q334262","Guercino was an Italian painter born in Cento in 1591. His nickname means the squinter, and his big, dramatic altarpieces are full of motion and strong light. He died in Bologna in 1666."),
("Q335927","Gerrit Dou was a Dutch painter born in Leiden in 1613. He was Rembrandt's first student, and became famous for tiny, polished pictures with glowing candlelight and very fine detail. He died in 1675."),
("Q336747","François Clouet was a French painter born in Tours around 1510. He was the court painter to several kings of France, and he painted neat, careful portraits and miniatures. He died in Paris in 1572."),
("Q336908","Meindert Hobbema was a Dutch landscape painter, born in Amsterdam in 1638. He is best known for peaceful pictures of country roads, watermills and trees. He died in 1709."),
("Q346952","Jan Gossaert was a Flemish painter born around 1478. He traveled to Italy and brought Renaissance ideas back to Flanders and the Netherlands, where he painted myths and portraits. He died in 1532."),
("Q348024","Carlo Crivelli was an Italian painter born in Venice in about 1430, who spent most of his life working in towns along the Adriatic coast. His altarpieces glitter with gold and jewels, and he liked to add painted fruit and flies. He died in about 1495."),
("Q352954","Carel Fabritius was a Dutch painter born in 1622, who studied with Rembrandt. He painted only a few pictures, and he was killed at the age of 32 when a gunpowder store exploded in Delft in 1654, destroying much of his work. The Goldfinch is his best-known picture."),
("Q355213","Gabriel Metsu was a Dutch painter born in Leiden in 1629. He painted quiet pictures of people reading and writing letters and shopping, in neat houses. He died in Amsterdam in 1667."),
("Q355406","Paulus Potter was a Dutch painter, born in 1625. He painted animals such as cows, horses and bulls, in a very true-to-life way, and died young, aged 28, in Amsterdam in 1654."),
("Q356777","Dosso Dossi was an Italian painter born around 1480, who worked for the dukes of Ferrara. His pictures are full of magic, mystery and bright colors. He died in 1542."),
("Q359421","Salvator Rosa was a painter, poet and actor born in Naples in 1615. He painted wild, rocky landscapes with bandits and witches, and was well known as a wild character in Rome. He died there in 1673."),
("Q360010","Pierre Mignard was a French painter born in Troyes in 1612. He was a favorite of Louis XIV, painted many portraits of him and became the first painter to the king. He died in Paris in 1695."),
("Q360888","Geertgen tot Sint Jans was a Dutch painter who was born in Leiden around 1460 and lived in a monastery in Haarlem, where his name means Little Gerard of the Brothers of Saint John. He died young, in his late twenties, around 1490."),
("Q367360","Orazio Gentileschi was an Italian painter, born in Pisa in 1563. He worked in Rome, Genoa, Paris and England, and he was the father and teacher of Artemisia Gentileschi. He died in London in 1639."),
("Q367895","Adriaen van Stalbemt was a Flemish painter born in Antwerp in 1580. He painted landscapes and scenes of collectors' rooms. He died in Antwerp in 1662."),
("Q368546","Domenico Veneziano was an Italian painter, born in Venice around 1410. He worked in Florence, and his paintings are known for their clear, pale and sunny colors. He died in 1461."),
("Q379521","Ercole de' Roberti was an Italian painter born in Ferrara around 1450. He worked for the ruling d'Este family and painted sharp, strangely charged scenes. He died in 1496."),
("Q380726","Reza Abbasi was a Persian painter, born in about 1565. He worked at the court of Shah Abbas the Great in Isfahan, and painted elegant figures in graceful lines. He died in 1635."),
("Q41264","Johannes Vermeer was a Dutch painter born in Delft in 1632. He painted calm scenes of women in sunlit rooms, with pearls, maps, letters and music, and made fewer than 40 paintings that we know of. He died in 1675, and he was almost forgotten until the 1800s."),
("Q42207","Caravaggio was an Italian painter born in 1571, whose real name was Michelangelo Merisi. He painted dramatic scenes lit by a strong beam of light with deep shadows and used ordinary people as models. He had a violent temper, had to flee Rome after a fight, and died in 1610."),
]
json.dump([list(r) for r in R],open("../out/old_artists_00.json","w"),ensure_ascii=False,indent=0)
print(len(R))
